.TH MS 1 "December 2025" "ms 1.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ms \- Modern ls command replacement with enhanced formatting and features
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ms
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fI/path/to/list\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ms
is a modern replacement for the traditional
.B ls
command, providing enhanced formatting, better color coding, and additional features for directory listing.
.PP
The command lists directory contents, categorizing files by type (directories, regular files, symbolic links, and special files) and displaying them with color coding and optional detailed information.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-long
Use a long listing format showing permissions, owner, group, size, and modification time.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-all
Show all files including those beginning with a dot (hidden files).
.TP
.B \-A, \-\-almost-all
Show all files except . and ...
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-reverse
Reverse the order of the sort.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-sort=\fItype\fR
Sort by
.IR type ,
where
.I type
is one of:
.RS
.TP
.B name
Sort alphabetically by filename (default).
.TP
.B size
Sort by file size.
.TP
.B time
Sort by modification time.
.TP
.B type
Sort by file type.
.RE
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-summary
Show a summary at the end showing counts of different file types.
.TP
.B \-H, \-\-human
Show sizes in human readable format (e.g., 1K, 2M, 3G).
.TP

.B \-k, \-\-tree
Display directory contents in tree view format.
.TP
.B \-K, \-\-tree-metadata
Display directory contents in tree view format with metadata (size and time).
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-table
Display files in table format showing name and size.
.TP
.B \-N, \-\-two-column
Display files in two-column format for better space utilization.
.TP
.B \-z, \-\-zebra
Display files with zebra striping (alternating row colors).
.TP
.B \-Z, \-\-zebra-metadata
Display files with zebra striping and metadata (size and time).
.TP
.B \-\-pattern=\fIpattern\fR
Filter files by pattern using wildcards (e.g., *.py, test_*).
.TP
.B \-\-time-format=\fIformat\fR
Specify custom time format (strftime format string).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information and exit.
.SH OUTPUT MODES
.PP
.B ms
supports multiple output formats:
.TP
.B List view (default)
Traditional file listing with optional long format.
.TP
.B Tree view (-k, -K)
Hierarchical tree-style display of directory contents.
.TP
.B Table view (-n)
Tabular format showing filename and size columns.
.TP
.B Two-column view (-N)
Efficient space utilization by displaying items in two columns.
.TP
.B Zebra view (-z, -Z)
Alternating row colors for improved readability.
.SH OUTPUT
.PP
.B ms
categorizes and displays files with color coding:
.TP
.B Blue
Directories
.TP
.B Cyan
Symbolic links
.TP
.B Magenta
Special files (devices, pipes, sockets)
.TP
.B Red
Large files (>1MB)
.TP
.B Yellow
Medium files (1KB-1MB)
.TP
.B White/Default
Small files and regular text
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLORS
Controls color output. If not set, colors are enabled by default if output is a terminal.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
List current directory:
.B ms
.TP
List with all details:
.B ms \-l /etc
.TP
List all files including hidden:
.B ms \-a
.TP
Sort by size, reverse order:
.B ms \-Sr \-\-long
.TP
Show Python files with summary:
.B ms \-\-pattern="*.py" \-s
.TP
Custom time format:
.B ms \-l \-\-time-format="%Y\-%m\-%d %H:%M"
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful completion
.TP
.B >0
An error occurred
.SH AUTHOR
Written by MiniMax Agent.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ls (1),
.BR find (1),
.BR stat (1)
.SH NOTES
.B ms
provides enhanced features over traditional
.B ls
including:
.IP
\(bu Better color coding for file types and sizes
.IP
\(bu Automatic categorization of files
.IP
\(bu Human readable size formatting
.IP
\(bu Pattern filtering
.IP
\(bu Summary statistics
.IP
\(bu Custom time formatting
.PP
The command is designed to be compatible with
.B ls
while providing additional functionality for modern use cases.